  "limits": [
    "Receipt/schema/count/execution checks, not automated quotation truth, historical authenticity or cultural permission.",
    "F counting reads receipts structurally at any nesting depth and counts distinct documents plus the retrieval units an aggregated receipt carries; a .md companion of a same-stem .json counts once. Disposition labels are read claim-level by tier with raw/prior/round-8 and per-element verdicts excluded, classified on the verdict head, and read fail-closed when same-tier labels disagree; primary/scholarly classification is regex-based and can misclassify an unusual source kind. When no round-9 reconciliation file exists, raw labels are read as receipt fields kept apart from a disposition reading rather than as a bound table.",
    "O digest checks recompute every pinned input against the bytes on disk (baseline-local snapshot first, repository path second); they do not execute the gates over the baselines -- the battery owns that, and its baseline coverage and tamper behaviour are read from its own run and selftest.",
